{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>The Gaon [Saadia] said,</b> that ויקרא לו אל אלהי ישראל means he called El 'the El of Israel.' But the correct interpretation is that this is the name of the altar, just as Moses named his altar 'YHWH Nissi' (Exodus 17:15) on account of the miracle that HaShem performed in that place, and likewise when the Shekhinah returns to Jerusalem it shall be called יהוה שָמָה (Ezekiel 48:35), and likewise because HaShem helped Jacob, he named the altar where he served HaShem 'El, the Elohim of Israel,' the reason being that He is strong and mighty:" "<b>The Elohim of Israel.</b> Who saved him on the way, and he came whole to the land of Canaan, for there are Shechem and Succoth. And in my opinion it is possible that he stayed in the city of Shechem for many years, for Dinah was not yet seven years old, and Simeon and Levi were young:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאון to Saadia per standard epithet convention; 'the reason being that He is strong and mighty' translates the final clause hyper-literally as it stands in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:59.717490132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}